# Known-good command names for the reject-obfuscated-commands hook, each with
# its write classification for the enforce-allowed-dirs hook.
# One entry per line: the name, whitespace, then exactly one of
#   read-only   the command writes no file named by its arguments
#   writer      it can create, replace, remove or re-mode a file named by its
#               arguments, or runs code that can (an interpreter, a runner,
#               a build tool); enforce-allowed-dirs checks its arguments as
#               write targets
# When in doubt, classify as writer: a read-only command's arguments are not
# checked at all. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
# Path-qualified invocations (/usr/bin/git, ./scripts/x, <hooks-path>/pre-commit)
# are matched by basename. A command that is not on this list (and not on
# command-blocklist, which wins) is rejected outright, and one without a valid
# classification is blocked by enforce-allowed-dirs - extend this file when a
# new tool is legitimately required, rather than changing hook logic.
# test/command-allowlist-parity.bats fails on an unclassified entry.
#
# NOTE: being listed here only means "not obfuscated and known-good by name".
# The claude-managed-settings.json permissions allow/deny layer still governs
# what a listed command may actually do.

ssh                                   read-only
# (scp deliberately excluded - no legitimate need for the agent's own Bash
# tool to transfer files directly; file movement in this repo's workflow
# goes through git, and scp's own [user@]host:path grammar was the source
# of two of #1315's confirmed hook bugs - see #1315 and enforce-ssh-host-
# and-key's header)

# Version control / forge
git                                   writer
gh                                    writer
# (gpg deliberately excluded - only used for commit signing, which git
# invokes internally via user.signingkey/commit.gpgsign; the agent's own
# Bash tool has no legitimate reason to run gpg directly, see #1315)
pre-commit                            writer
pre-commit-check                      writer

